      "results": [
        {
          "id": "ff3919a7aecf66d4113ecfab1a1fe6b0",
          "text": "It also allows disabling automatic exception chaining using the from None idiom:\n\n>>> try:\n...     open('database.sqlite')\n... except OSError:\n...     raise RuntimeError from None\n...\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 4, in <module>\n    raise RuntimeError from None\nRuntimeError\n\nFor more information about chaining mechanics, see Built-in Exceptions.",
          "source_id": "python-3.14-ch08",
          "source": "https://docs.python.org/3.14/tutorial/errors.html",
          "page": "python-3.14-ch08-u005",
          "metadata": {
            "chapter": 8,
            "version": "3.14.10",
            "char_end": 1199,
            "language": "en",
