            ],
            "unit_char_start_in_chapter": 10179,
            "document_id": "python-3.14-ch08",
            "source": "https://docs.python.org/3.14/tutorial/errors.html",
            "page": "python-3.14-ch08-u005"
          },
          "score": 0.8546347618103027,
          "strategy": "dense"
        },
        {
          "id": "b7ede215f2ba3869fbe2469c31434a76",
          "text": "Note that the exceptions nested in an exception group must be instances, not types. This is because in practice the exceptions would typically be ones that have already been raised and caught by the program, along the following pattern:\n\n>>> excs = []\n>>> for test in tests:\n...     try:\n...         test.run()\n...     except Exception as e:\n...         excs.append(e)\n...\n>>> if excs:\n...    raise ExceptionGroup(\"Test Failures\", excs)\n...",
          "source_id": "python-3.14-ch08",
          "source": "https://docs.python.org/3.14/tutorial/errors.html",
          "page": "python-3.14-ch08-u008",
          "metadata": {
